Yeenoghu does respect Elbereth, so if you've got Magicbane already,
engraving it a few dozen times on the upstair *might* allow
you to beat him.  Just be sure to engrave it just once the first
time, then add to it once you're safe. Otherwise he'll interrupt
you.

Don't do this unless you have some means of dealing damage quickly
though. Even if he can't retaliate directly, he can still summon
Demogorgon if you give him enough time, and then you'll have a
*really* irritating bones file to deal with.

It's risky even discounting that, so definitely go to Minetown
first and see if you can find a magic lamp. SDSM would make this
strategy much more likely to succeed even if the E square gets
damaged.  And Mine's End is probably worth doing, too.  If
Yeenoghu summons nasties, it'll be just as bad as anything you
find down there, and the extra XP would be potentially helpful,
as would the luckstone if you #offer enough to get your luck
high.

Oh, and the minetown captain usually has a silver saber. Quite
effective against demons if you can get your pet to take him out.
(or are willing to accept the penalty for murder)

Good luck.


